From e3edaaf706206f1ae6ea9c79f72767960e9bae34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Pukhov <alex.m.pukhov@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:23:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] openPMD reader: rectilinear meshes (explicit grid
 coordinates)

Meshes with explicit, non-equidistant coordinates along some axes, as proposed
for openPMD 2.0 (openPMD-standard issue #142, PR #299: mesh attribute
gridCoordinates naming one 1D coordinate data set per axis, '' for a regular
axis), are read as vtkRectilinearGrid (cartesian), and thetaMode meshes use the
explicit radial and longitudinal node positions in their vtkStructuredGrid.

- coordinate data sets are read with openPMD-api if it supports them
  (Iteration.grid_coordinates), otherwise from HDF5 files with h5py; if neither
  is available the reader warns and falls back to gridSpacing
- also reads the interim form of openPMD 1.1 files (attribute
  gridCoordinates_<axis label>, written by QUARZ) and thetaMode meshes marked
  as geometry 'other' with geometryParameters 'thetaMode;...'
- regular meshes are unchanged (vtkImageData)
- piece requests slice the coordinates with the extent

Tested with the vtk Python package (no ParaView GUI): QUARZ native output,
synthetic cartesian 3D/2D files (both axis orders) and thetaMode files, with
released openPMD-api + h5py and with openPMD-api with coordinate data sets;
point coordinates and values agree with an independent h5py reader to
round-off; regular files unchanged.
